    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5360" root="جذم" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَامٌ</span></b>  [an epithet] of the measure <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَعَّالٌ</span> from
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الجَذْمُ</span> meaning <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">القَطْعُ</span>: so in the phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَذَّامُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَبْلِ الهَوَى</span> [<i>Wont to sever the bond of love</i>], in a
verse of Ows Ibn-Thaalabeh. (Ham p. 334.)

